 ('ENT_URA_TUSHPUEA','spouse_of','ENT_URA_SHIVINI','low','Listed third in the female-deity sequence paralleling Shivini; taken as his consort; the capital Tushpa derives from her name.',''),
 ('ENT_URA_HUBA','spouse_of','ENT_URA_TEISHEBA','medium','Huba is paired with the storm-god Teisheba as his consort.',''),
 ('ENT_URA_HUBA','aligned_with','ENT_HTT_HEPAT','high','Urartian Huba corresponds to Hurrian Hepat, consort of Teshub, consistent with Teisheba being the Urartian Teshub.',''),
 ('ENT_URA_SARDI','presides_over','ENT_SUN','low','Sardi is the Urartian astral/star deity; anchored to the nearest celestial-luminary abstraction.',''),
 ('ENT_URA_SPEAR_KHALDI','embodies','ENT_WAR','high','The lance of Khaldi is the war-god''s sacred weapon, credited with victory on the Karagunduz stele.',''),
 ('ENT_URA_SPEAR_KHALDI','guardian_of','ENT_URA_KHALDI','high','The spear is the cult weapon of Khaldi, stored in his temples as the instrument of his victories.',''),
 ('ENT_IB_COSUS','presides_over','ENT_WAR','high','Cosus is a war-god of NW Hispania, equated with Mars via interpretatio romana.',''),
